  "limitations": [
    "No Stripe credential, sandbox, test/live account, webhook, Events page, balance-transaction page, provider rate limit, or permission denial was exercised. The exact app manifest, balance_transaction_source_read and implied permissions, direct/destination-charge behavior, and provider contract remain owner-review and sandbox requirements.",
    "The source-defined PostgreSQL integration test was not executed because the restricted-role URLs, .env, and local PostgreSQL runtime were absent. Receipt/classification/outbox/canonical atomicity, RLS, role privileges, tenant concealment, and query behavior remain unverified at runtime for this increment.",
    "Stripe documents asynchronous balance-transaction creation. Periodic gap-repair convergence, overlap/cadence selection, late availability, settlement finality, pagination completeness, and provider-wide fee coverage are not proven by local tests.",
    "Interchange-plus fee retrieval is explicitly unsupported. A Charge without a PaymentIntent remains incomplete and must not be treated as a deterministic payment link.",
    "An older worker cannot read stripe-v2 cursors. Mixed-image drain, process loss at the phase boundary, rollback, duplicate overlapping windows, representative volume/timing, managed Redis, dashboards, silence behavior, alert delivery, and protected staging remain unverified.",
    "The minimized snapshot intentionally does not preserve the full provider response. It preserves selected replay/provenance evidence but is not proof of every Stripe object field or future API compatibility.",
    "A balance_transaction observed watermark proves only immutable intake. It does not prove normalization success, completed two-phase pagination, current provider availability, fee completeness, settlement finality, or reconciliation correctness."
  ]
